@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# Private local patch candidate
+
+This package is a privately maintained derivative of npm `braces@3.0.3`,
+not an upstream release or an independently certified security fix.
+Its upstream MIT license and attribution are retained.
+
+The published advisory GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm describes uncontrolled recursion
+and has no listed upstream fixed version at the time of this assessment.
+
+Local changes:
+
+- String parsing enforces a non-configurable limit of 64 nested containers.
+- Compile, stringify, and expand also accept existing AST objects. Their
+  internal entry points now inspect child edges iteratively before recursion,
+  rejecting child cycles and depths above 65 edges. The extra edge permits
+  leaf nodes beneath 64 parsed containers.
+- Expansion's parent-chain walks have a fixed hop limit as well.
+- The validator expects AST child lists to be arrays. Parser-produced cyclic
+  parent/previous backlinks are deliberately excluded from child traversal.
+
+Limits are intentional compatibility restrictions. This patch is not a general
+resource quota for expansion cardinality, arbitrary getters/proxies, or all
+possible JavaScript objects. Existing expansion range limits are unchanged.
+
+The standalone regression probe is explicitly skipped by owner instruction.
+No replacement or stress/boundary probes are authorized. The earlier ordinary
+root install/lint/typecheck/build results apply to the previous parser-only
+candidate, not automatically to this revision. Further ordinary validation is
+required before integration. Registry audit inventory for a renamed private
+package is not evidence that its implementation is safe.
